Hello PDAX Team,

At Edukasyon.ph, we=E2=80=99re all about journey-ing with the Filipino yo=
uth to
navigate student life and figure out their next big steps. But a huge par=
t
of that journey happens outside the textbooks.

As we celebrate Pride Month, we=E2=80=99re looking at how the gender disc=
ourse
actually plays out inside classrooms and campuses. Why? Because the
students navigating these spaces today are the very talent, leaders, and
change-makers entering your workplaces tomorrow.

If we want to build inclusive industries, we need to understand where our
future workforce is coming from. Are they getting the support they need?
Are their mentors equipped to guide them?  That=E2=80=99s why we=E2=80=99=
re doing EDK Club
Time: Crossroad Conversations=E2=80=94and we=E2=80=99d love for your team=
, HR leaders, and
DEI advocates to hang out with us!

What=E2=80=99s the vibe? [image: :sparkles:]
Our goal isn=E2=80=99t to debate or force anyone to take sides. We=E2=80=
=99re just meeting
at the crossroads for a genuine, human, and respectful chat to better
understand each other. Think of it as a safe, relaxed, and strictly
judgment-free virtual hangout. Your team can openly share insights, or
simply tune in and listen like a live podcast.

Event Details:
[image: :spiral_calendar_pad:] Friday, June 26
[image: :clock4:] 4:00 PM
[image: :computer:] Via Google Meet

How do we join?
Locking in your *FREE* slots is super easy. You can check out the full
details in the attached primer or register directly through the link belo=
w:
[image: :point_right:] go.edukasyon.ph/edkclubtimejune

We=E2=80=99d be thrilled to have your organization=E2=80=99s voice in thi=
s conversation as
we bridge the gap between inclusive education and inclusive workplaces!

See you at the crossroads,
[image: image.png]

SOPHIA MABANSAG

AWS re/Start HR Generalist

Ayala Triangle Gardens Tower One Building,

Ayala Avenue, Makati City 1229

+63 976 491 0695

